 ## Background
-The method originates from the need to hybridize ray tracing and volume rendering. Early hybrid ray tracers used binary voxel representations for polyhedra and parametric surfaces, resulting in aliasing [S1, unofficial]. To avoid these artifacts, Kaufman et al. proposed bandlimiting objects to the Nyquist frequency and using volume rendering's partial opacity to handle the resulting voxel representation [S1, unofficial]. This approach allows polygons to be shaded, filtered, sampled, and combined with volumetric data, which is then rendered using standard techniques without supersampling [S1, unofficial]. The work is documented in the DTIC report ADA208091 [S1, unofficial].
